    "intro_html":  "Massaman is the gentlest of the Thai curries and the one with the longest passport. It came into southern Thailand through Persian and Indian traders, which is why it carries potatoes and peanuts and a sweetness that the other curries do not have. It is thick, mild enough that kids will eat it, and it is basically a stew wearing a curry\u0027s clothes. Each serving lands at \u003cstrong\u003e668 calories and 30 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$2.34\u003c/strong\u003e.",
